{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0HA6", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-excellent}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:62448a9983bdc013c96b94101c573b42b0b17b4fef7a2a615323350cf7a4e77d", "source_text": "Excellent schemes", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a0a34e496705b60a0efce6aca89d2bb9041d27f0ad6f128689b3e076c1bb66b2", "unit_id": "tag:0HA6:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0HA6", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:42ea0d787afd9d3b2ba2bb5aa33cc0b2d37b3cbc104b07e3284ac21281cf80e5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe recall that a ring is quasi-excellent if it is a G-ring and J-2.\nA ring is excellent if it is quasi-excellent and universally catenary.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:285986b014a5936d496b104d41b8310c96de1608249a4c24b4e778f7fdc15f57", "unit_id": "tag:0HA6:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0HA6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$x \\in U \\subset X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0008": "$x \\in U \\subset X$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{more-algebra-definition-excellent}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{more-algebra-definition-excellent}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-excellent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ff37bbdd1e3be0cca898b7dc940592d462df66285d6d0690bbf878fdb59d32ee", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:60aa8bd1655c8ea45b551dc95b83bf313b38ed7b2dd0f178ec8ebc0ec40aef2a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> We say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>quasi-excellent<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if for every <MATH_0003> there exists\nan affine open neighbourhood <MATH_0004> such that the ring\n<MATH_0005> is quasi-excellent (see\nMore on Algebra, Definition <REF_0001>).\n<STRUCT_0003> We say <MATH_0006> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>excellent<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if for every <MATH_0007> there exists an\naffine open neighbourhood <MATH_0008> such that the ring\n<MATH_0009> is excellent (see\nMore on Algebra, Definition <REF_0002>).\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c644dea0394543c2fe311cdc30c26a4f13eb62370e41f30f3e4b29753d956356", "unit_id": "tag:0HA7:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0HA6", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:42ea0d787afd9d3b2ba2bb5aa33cc0b2d37b3cbc104b07e3284ac21281cf80e5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nQuasi-excellent schemes are locally Noetherian (G-rings are Noetherian).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d5fe6b8c7b22dddcfab2d2888ad5c005867b3d8a643b8f8f56cc123919992d9f", "unit_id": "tag:0HA6:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0HA6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-quasi-excellent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:b3055ea2944ed5fcda6131396aa9e9e6d3ca5169ca39bc6c9f17b2efc3c1e8ce", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1b2518682112aa0541e9f2af993d3c66266713d492314f2ad6e636402f39c0c4", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. The following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is quasi-excellent, and\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0003> is a G-scheme and J-2.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7da557edc223c19af18282dd922895df52530c0b4d077ac3b07a91292a968333", "unit_id": "tag:0HA8:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0HA6", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Rightarrow$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$x \\in U \\subset X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X(U)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-excellent}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{more-algebra-definition-excellent}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{properties-definition-G-scheme}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-J}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{lemma-J}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d13d649f178f29f4757e9aa72df501892cb6856e6ea9cdcb15692ad1a66ceca1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0b35d4ee16e0ecfc964e3c518ce910ad8cf7b8276cdadc0816f037fd1bffd68d", "source_text": "The implication (1) <MATH_0001> (2) follows on combining\nthe definition of quasi-excellent schemes\n(Definition <REF_0001>),\nthe definition of quasi-excellent rings\n(More on Algebra, Definition <REF_0002>),\nthe definition of G-schemes\n(Properties, Definition <REF_0003>), and\nLemma <REF_0004>.\nConversely, if <MATH_0002> is a G-scheme and J-2, then for any <MATH_0003>\nwe can find an affine open neighbourhood <MATH_0004>\nsuch that <MATH_0005> is a G-ring. By Lemma <REF_0005>\nthe ring <MATH_0006> is also J-2, whence quasi-excellent.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:842a6f9a2096d978e8c9b5665a64cab8526a9cd8d506b276c5a25f43ae13c7ea", "unit_id": "tag:0HA8:proof"}
